* cs03.input - asking the person at the terminal for values
*
* input waits for a line and puts it in a variable.  prompt sets the character input shows first ('' for none).
* A number typed is still text until it is used as a number; num() says whether it can be.

program cs03.input
   prompt ''
   crt 'What is your name? ' :               ;* a : at the end keeps the cursor on the same line
   input name
   crt 'How old are you? ' :
   input age
   if not(num(age)) or age = '' then
      crt 'That is not a number, ' : name : '.'
      stop
   end
   crt 'Hello, ' : name : '.  In ten years you will be ' : age + 10 : '.'
end
